.TH FANCTLD 8 "2026" "acer-predator-ph315-51-fan-control" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
fanctld \- fan control daemon for the Acer Predator PH315-51
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fanctld
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B fanctld
runs as root and writes the Acer Predator PH315-51 embedded
controller's fan registers directly through
.IR /sys/kernel/debug/ec/ec0/io ,
which requires root and the
.B ec_sys
kernel module loaded with
.B write_support=1
(see
.IR /usr/lib/modprobe.d/ec_sys.conf
and
.IR /usr/lib/modules-load.d/ec_sys.conf ).
.PP
It listens on the Unix socket
.I /run/fanctld.sock
for the newline-terminated commands \fBstatus\fR, \fBfull\fR and
\fBauto\fR, and replies with a single line of JSON. The socket is
created mode 0660 and owned by the UID/GID configured via the
.B FANCTLD_UID
and
.B FANCTLD_GID
environment variables (both default to 1000), so only that local user
can connect \(em no client-side privilege is required or granted.
.PP
Intended to run under systemd; see the shipped
.I fanctld.service
unit. Use
.B systemctl edit fanctld.service
to override
.B FANCTLD_UID
/
.B FANCTLD_GID
if your desktop user isn't UID 1000.
.SH WARNING
The register offsets and values this daemon writes were observed
specifically on the Acer Predator PH315-51 embedded controller. They
are not known to be correct or safe on other hardware.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /run/fanctld.sock
Control socket.
.TP
.I /sys/kernel/debug/ec/ec0/io
Embedded controller register I/O, via the ec_sys kernel module.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fanctl (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Yaroslav Yushchenko
